From 6a296a4658124490d7dddd2b751e5f9ae5c5aec7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Luiz Augusto von Dentz <luiz.von.dentz@intel.com>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 16:16:07 -0500
Subject: Bluetooth: hci_core: Take req_sync lock in hci_power_on()
Git-commit: 6a296a4658124490d7dddd2b751e5f9ae5c5aec7
Patch-mainline: v7.4-rc5
References: git-fixes

hci_powered_update_sync() issues synchronous HCI commands but was called
without hci_req_sync_lock(), racing with other request users.

Reported-by: Sashiko <sashiko-bot@kernel.org>
Link: https://sashiko.dev/#/bug/linux-1baf7393-3aeb-4fa5-806f-19cea743b9f3
Fixes: cf75ad8b41d2 ("Bluetooth: hci_sync: Convert MGMT_SET_POWERED")
Assisted-by: OpenCode:claude-fable-5.2
Signed-off-by: Luiz Augusto von Dentz <luiz.von.dentz@intel.com>
Acked-by: Takashi Iwai <tiwai@suse.de>

---
 net/bluetooth/hci_core.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/net/bluetooth/hci_core.c b/net/bluetooth/hci_core.c
index 846e6eb2d1bc..f0e23b59b600 100644
--- a/net/bluetooth/hci_core.c
+++ b/net/bluetooth/hci_core.c
@@ -915,7 +915,9 @@ static void hci_power_on(struct work_struct *work)
 	    hci_dev_test_flag(hdev, HCI_MGMT) &&
 	    hci_dev_test_and_clear_flag(hdev, HCI_AUTO_OFF)) {
 		cancel_delayed_work(&hdev->power_off);
+		hci_req_sync_lock(hdev);
 		err = hci_powered_update_sync(hdev);
+		hci_req_sync_unlock(hdev);
 		mgmt_power_on(hdev, err);
 		return;
 	}
-- 
